.vscode/**
.backups/**
.git/**
.gitignore
src/**
test/**
python/test_*.py
# Reporter output, wherever it lands. `demo/logs/**` alone was not enough: the reporter
# writes to <repo>/logs the moment anyone runs a script against the working copy, and 1.6.1
# shipped 9 of those files -- the OS username and an internal commit SHA -- to the Marketplace.
# vsce packages from the FILESYSTEM, not from git, so .gitignore does not protect this.
**/logs/**
scripts/**
node_modules/**
tsconfig.json
*.vsix
dist/**
out/**/*.map
**/__pycache__/**
docs/**
.harness/**
ROADMAP.md
PUBLISHING.md
.github/**
demo/*.py
install/**
*.code-workspace
